Services of GNU/seL4, for s6-rc (https://skarnet.org/software/s6-rc/).

source/<name>/type      oneshot (runs once: "up", "down") or longrun (supervised: "run")
source/<name>/dependencies.d/<other>   start <other> first
source/default          the bundle brought up at boot

/etc/rc compiles source/ into /run/s6-rc/db at every boot (s6-rc-compile), starts s6-rc on
the s6-svscan scan directory /run/service and brings "default" up. At run time:
  s6-rc -a list              services that are up
  s6-rc -u change NAME       bring NAME (and what it depends on) up; -d brings it down
  s6-svstat /run/service/NAME   state of a longrun; s6-svc -r restarts it
